            <ArticleTitle>Chest discomfort in a patient with cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-4, 466</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.JAA.0000464279.28870.3b</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with cancer are at higher risk for venous thromboembolism than patients without cancer due to hypercoagulability associated with malignancy. This article describes a patient with metastatic renal cell carcinoma who had chest pain over several weeks caused by multiple pulmonary emboli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
